{
  "_comment": [
    "Apps the Android shield keeps OUT of its VPN tunnel (AppExclusions.kt).",
    "PROPOSAL — the founder decides which entries are default:true. default:true = excluded on every phone that has the app;",
    "default:false = not excluded, only offered at the top of the 'app asks to turn off the VPN' picker.",
    "Excluding an app means its own DNS (including its built-in browser) is NOT filtered. Never list a browser.",
    "Every package name must also be in the module AndroidManifest <queries> (AppExclusionsTest pins it):",
    "without package visibility the shield cannot tell whether the app is installed.",
    "package_source: where the package name was confirmed (RuStore catalog URL = the app's official listing).",
    "certain:false = the package name is not confirmed from an official listing; check before relying on it.",
    "vpn_evidence: a report that the app refuses or limits use while a VPN is on (empty = none found, listed for other reasons)."
